  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For isoelectronic species higher the $\\frac{\\mathrm{Z}}{\\mathrm{e}}$ ratio, smaller the ionic radius\n$\\frac{z}{e}$ for\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{O}^{2-}=\\frac{8}{10}=0.8 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~F}^{-}=\\frac{9}{10}=0.9 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Na}^{+}=\\frac{11}{10}=1.1 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}=\\frac{12}{10}=1.2 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Al}^{3+}=\\frac{13}{10}=1.3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
